			},
			"date": "2022-12-11T02:51:57.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@coryd\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>coryd</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> it was a “manual” machine where you had to spin a wheel (or use a back/forth pedal) to make it run. Newer machines are probably electric, and less reliable.</p><p>According to my mom, electric machines are also worse since they give you less control.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109492811388870033",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://social.jacobian.org/@jacob/109492811345255397",
			"author": {
				"name": "jacobian",
				"url": "https://social.jacobian.org/@jacob",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/287/922/999/525/044/original/2539cbe9539408ab.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2022-12-11T03:01:52.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I have a brother SE400, which is a combo sewing and embroidery machine. The embroidery features are super cool: you can program in patterns and it stitches them — essentially a CNC sewing machine. And as a sewing machine it’s been really solid and easy to use. I think it (or the bigger SE600) is a really great all-around machine for most people.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
